  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing the EU-Australia Partnership on Sustainable Critical and Strategic Minerals</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The EU-Australia strategic partnership on CRM aims to support several common objectives, while based on mutual benefits. It seeks to enable the EU to diversify its supplies of materials necessary for the green and digital transitions, whilst contributing to the development of Australia&#xbf;s domestic critical minerals sector. The partnership covers the entire critical and strategic minerals value chain: exploration, extraction, processing, refining, recycling, and processing of extractive waste.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The overall objective of this Action, in line with the goals of the EU CRM Act is to make a substantial contribution to a stable, diversified, and sustainable supply chain of critical raw materials for the EU by promoting its partnership with Australia, a resource-rich and like-minded country with strong ESG credentials, in research and innovation and business creation. The specific objectives of this Action are to fast-track the execution of the roadmap for the implementation of the EU-Australia strategic partnership on CRM/SRMs, and more precisely to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Increase economic and industrial integration between EU and Australia in the sustainable and strategic value chain of critical minerals&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Promote the exchange of good practice on ESG standards, research and innovation in the minerals sector&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
